      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fa30b66b36d4b12af626dc8|full_name}: I noticed that issue in one of my worlds I am still working on, it's a private world.\n\nBut I just uploaded a small world where the issue can be reproduced : https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_6c3f904e-9eda-427f-bdf3-c486afecaed7\n\nThe code that breaks :\n\n```\n\npublic class ForVRChat : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n\tpublic Animator MyAnimator;\n\n    void Start()\n\n    {\n\n\t\tMyAnimator.keepAnimatorControllerStateOnDisable = true;\n\n\t}\n\n}\n\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-30T14:59:00.008Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "One of my worlds uses the animator property `animator.keepAnimatorControllerStateOnDisable`, which breaks my scripts in Unity 2022 because that property is obsolete and got replaced with `keepAnimatorStateOnDisable`, the error message is `Function '__set_keepAnimatorControllerStateOnDisable__SystemBoolean__SystemVoid' is not implemented yet`.\n\nLink to the documentation : https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Animator-keepAnimatorControllerStateOnDisable.html\n\nIn my particular case, it is not a big issue because I am still updating my worlds, and I'll do it once the 2022 SDK gets released, but this issue might break older worlds that do not get updated anymore.",
